## 4. Conclusions
We have demonstrated an effective strategy to synthesize a series of Al-MIL-101 analogues by simply adjusting the molar ratio of Fe to Al in the precursor solution. In addition, these Al-MIL-101 analogues have different morphologies, sizes, surface areas, and different phosphorus adsorption capacities. Al-MIL-101 analogues synthesized by this method contained only Al and no Fe. As expected, the optimized Fe/Al (0.5) exhibited excellent phosphate removal performance, including a remarkable absorption capacity, relatively fast adsorption rate, broad working pH range, strong phosphorous selectivity, excellent regeneration, and excellent phosphorus removal from natural water samples. In summary, this study showed the rational design of Al-MIL-101 analogues with adjustable structures and ideal functions, and also shows that they can be used to treat polluted water.
